      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test. The key understandability issues are: `yoe` is an opaque abbreviation, `base` and `era` don't signal expected vs. actual, the ternary logic is uncommented, and the class is cluttered with data-provider methods that no test in this class uses.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactoring improves understandability by renaming `year` → `prolepticYear`, `base` → `julianDate`, `era` → `expectedEra`, `yoe` → `expectedYearOfEra`, and `eraBased` → `eraBasedDate`, adding comments that explain the BC/AD boundary and the year-of-era counting convention, and removing the unused data-provider methods that were dead code in this single-test class."
